<div class="page prose">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lede" lang="uk">FotoDumky — це колекція думок, висловлених фотографією.</p>
  <p>FotoDumky is a collection of thoughts expressed through photography. The photograph is the carrier; the thought is the unit. They are not separable — a FotoDumka is what happens when both arrive at once.</p>
  <p>This is not a portfolio. Nothing here is for hire. The photographs are not illustrations of the sentences, and the sentences are not captions for the photographs. Sometimes the thought is philosophical, sometimes it is a joke, sometimes it is only two words. Some photographs are allowed to say nothing at all.</p>
  <p>The name joins <em>foto</em> — photograph — with <em>dumky</em>, the Ukrainian word for thoughts. The Ukrainian originals stay on the page, because the thought was born in that language; the English versions try to carry the idea rather than the words.</p>
  <p>What this collection asks of you is small: stop for a moment, look, and see what it makes <em>you</em> think.</p>
</div>
